# Project memory

Before planning, quoting, or changing product behavior, read:

- `docs/memory/DEVELOPMENT-BRIEF.md` — canonical product and commercial reference
- `docs/memory/BRIEF.md` — working summary
- `docs/memory/DECISIONS.md` — locked choices and open kickoff items
- `docs/memory/LOG.md` — work already done
- `docs/TIMELINE.md` — done, in progress, and pending through 30 Apr 2027

When a new fact, decision, or finished piece of work appears, update the matching file in the same change. Append `LOG.md`. Do not ask the user to repeat something already written there.

A newer explicit instruction from the user wins. Then update the files so they match.

Keep `.cursor/rules/` aligned when stack, structure, or phase scope changes. Update the six-month canvas when `docs/TIMELINE.md` status changes.

```markdown
<!-- docs/memory/LOG.md -->
## 12 Nov 2026
- Locked Next.js and Expo in DECISIONS and moved December scaffold to in progress.
```
